  "aerfala-bestiary": {
    "text": "# Aerfála Bestiary\n\nAerfála's creatures belong to living habitats, food webs, economies, and local cultures. Predators hunt prey, herbivores migrate, scavengers follow death, monsters compete for territory, dungeon spawn follows Deepgate's established rules, and constructs or undead persist through the concrete magic that sustains them. A creature exists where its biology, origin, migration, summoning, breeding, dungeon generation, or actual movement places it—not merely because the player entered a scene.\n\n## Encounter and Knowledge Rules\n- Listed levels describe typical healthy specimens. Age, injury, mutation, pack size, training, habitat, dungeon depth, and established magic change an individual without granting arbitrary boss immunity.\n- Temperament follows hunger, nesting, fear, territory, injury, domestication, magical influence, and prior contact. Wildlife flees, watches, feeds, fights, mates, sleeps, migrates, or ignores travelers according to circumstance.\n- Identification requires sight, tracks, remains, expertise, records, local knowledge, magic with an established scope, or another real information path. Seeing a creature does not reveal its name, level, abilities, weaknesses, origin, or loot automatically.\n- Creature abilities resolve through actual stats, ranks, positioning, resistances, conditions, and rolls. Names such as basilisk, leviathan, or aberrant grant no hidden immunity.\n- Signature loot enters play only when physically obtained. A kill does not automatically place intact materials in inventory. Damage, harvesting skill, tools, time, decomposition, contamination, law, ownership, and local custom determine condition and quantity.\n- Natural sheds, molts, antlers, feathers, secretions, nests, and remains exist without killing. Hunting pressure changes local populations, prices, predator behavior, and prey numbers. Rare or mythic creatures do not respawn merely to replenish loot.\n- Ordinary meat, bone, hide, fat, organs, and trophies exist when anatomy and condition support them. Signature loot below names the material with a dedicated Items entry; it does not erase ordinary physical remains.\n- Guild rank affects legal commissions, pay, clearance, and institutional response. It does not physically prevent an adventurer from encountering a stronger creature outside Guild authority.\n\n## Solasreach Plains, Rivers, and Lake\n\n### Dawnfield Hare\n- **Habitat:** Solasreach fields and orchard margins\n- **Typical Level:** 1–3\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A swift golden-brown grazer that trims weeds between crops and spreads clover seed through farm hedges. It freezes flat when shadowed, then escapes in violent zigzags.\n- **Combat Traits:** speed, burrow escape, sharp hearing; rarely attacks except when cornered.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Dawnfield Softfur**.\n\n### Grainback Boar\n- **Habitat:** Solasreach cropland, wooded hills, and neglected estates\n- **Typical Level:** 4–10\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A broad wild boar with wheat-colored bristles and a habit of rooting through mana-rich fields after harvest. Farmers tolerate small sounders because they turn soil and eat crop pests; a large sounder can ruin a season overnight.\n- **Combat Traits:** armored shoulders, straight charge, tusk sweep, stubborn pain tolerance.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Grainback Tusk**.\n\n### Riverglass Otter\n- **Habitat:** Solasreach rivers, Silverfen, and tributaries toward Bréanriv\n- **Typical Level:** 3–8\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A social blue-grey otter whose oiled guard hairs catch sunlight like broken glass. Colonies keep river mussels and invasive mana-snails in check and steal unattended fish with cheerful professionalism.\n- **Combat Traits:** fast swimming, coordinated distraction, slippery hide, biting retreat.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Riverglass Pelt**.\n\n### Suncrest Cockatrice\n- **Habitat:** abandoned Solasreach orchards, sun-warmed ruins, and Hollow Cathedral hills\n- **Typical Level:** 12–20\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A fox-sized feathered reptile with a copper crest that feeds on stone beetles and orchard vermin. Its territorial display drives livestock into panic, making culls common near farms.\n- **Combat Traits:** blinding crest-flare, muscle-stiffening gaze at close range, venomous spur, darting leaps; its gaze is resistible and never an unexplained instant kill.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Suncrest Spur**.\n\n### Grifonmere Lake Serpent\n- **Habitat:** deep Lake Grifon and flooded limestone channels\n- **Typical Level:** 20–32\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A long silver-blue freshwater predator that follows fish migrations and surfaces during pressure changes. Adults avoid crowded harbors unless spawning, injured, or drawn by dumped magical waste.\n- **Combat Traits:** coil strike, wake burst, deep dive, scale-shedding decoy, strong resistance to cold water.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Grifonmere Serpent Scale**.\n\n### Pale Steppe Charger\n- **Habitat:** The Pale Steppes of western Solasreach\n- **Typical Level:** 6–14\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A tall ash-white wild horse adapted to long dry runs and sudden grassland storms. Herds follow old salt routes and remain difficult to domesticate without patient handling rather than domination.\n- **Combat Traits:** sustained speed, herd wheel, rear kick, storm sense; flees before fighting.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Pale Charger Mane**.\n\n## Dúnbheal Mountains and Deep Halls\n\n### Orehide Ram\n- **Habitat:** Dúnbheal mountain slopes and abandoned quarry terraces\n- **Typical Level:** 6–14\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A squat ram whose horn ridges accumulate trace metal from mineral licks. Herds break loose scree, expose shallow veins, and warn miners of unstable slopes by abandoning them hours before collapse.\n- **Combat Traits:** rock-footed charge, horn lock, excellent balance, mineral-scenting.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Orehide Horn Core**.\n\n### Furnace Salamander\n- **Habitat:** Emberfall vents, Magma Wells, and warm forge drainage\n- **Typical Level:** 8–18\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A black-and-orange amphibian that grazes heat-loving algae around vents and nests where stone stays just below melting. Dwarven bathkeepers value small colonies because they consume sulfur scum.\n- **Combat Traits:** heat immunity, scalding skin, ember spit, tail-drop escape.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Furnace Salamander Gland**.\n\n### Frostvein Roc\n- **Habitat:** Frostvein Pass and the highest Dúnbheal peaks\n- **Typical Level:** 18–30\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A massive slate-feathered raptor that hunts mountain goats and carries ore-bright stones to decorate inaccessible nests. It rides blizzards rather than sheltering from them.\n- **Combat Traits:** high-altitude dive, wing-blast, prey lift, snowblind camouflage.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Frostvein Roc Pinion**.\n\n### Magma Burrower\n- **Habitat:** deep volcanic tunnels beneath Emberfall and the Magma Wells\n- **Typical Level:** 20–35\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A plated worm-beast that eats hot basalt and leaves porous, mineral-rich tunnels behind. Its migration opens geothermal vents; blocking one can redirect dangerous heat toward inhabited halls.\n- **Combat Traits:** stone burrow, magma spray, plated coil, tremor sense.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Magma Burrower Plate**.\n\n### Deepstone Basilisk\n- **Habitat:** sealed lower mines and caverns near the Obsidian Gates\n- **Typical Level:** 28–40\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A six-legged subterranean reptile that regulates crystal-eating cave vermin and nests in abandoned ore chambers. Its mineralizing gaze evolved to immobilize prey against cave walls, leaving the famous stone silhouettes miners fear.\n- **Combat Traits:** progressive mineralizing gaze, armored hide, crushing bite, darkness vision; petrification requires exposure and resistance resolution.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Deepstone Basilisk Lens**.\n\n### Khad Varr Gear Warden\n- **Habitat:** Ruins of Khad Varr\n- **Typical Level:** 25–38\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A pre-Collapse dwarven construct still following sealed patrol routes. It repairs doors, removes rubble, and attacks anyone its broken authorization lattice classifies as an intruder; it neither breeds nor belongs to the natural food web.\n- **Combat Traits:** modular limbs, rotating shield, forge-beam, tireless patrol, command-rune vulnerabilities.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Warden Gearheart**.\n\n## Scáthfenn Marshlands\n\n### Lantern Toad\n- **Habitat:** Scáthfenn pools, boardwalk ditches, and witch gardens\n- **Typical Level:** 2–6\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A dinner-plate-sized toad with a pale throat lantern used to attract insects through fog. Locals keep them near homes because their calls change before water rises.\n- **Combat Traits:** sticky tongue, startling light pulse, toxin-resistant skin, powerful leap.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Lantern Toad Glow-Sac**.\n\n### Mirejaw Crocodile\n- **Habitat:** deep Scáthfenn channels and flooded ruins\n- **Typical Level:** 8–18\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A broad black-green ambush predator that keeps boar, giant fish, and careless travelers from overusing the same crossings. Mirehaven hunters mark active nesting banks rather than trying to eradicate them.\n- **Combat Traits:** submerged ambush, death roll, armored back, explosive shore rush.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Mirejaw Scute**.\n\n### Corpse-Reed Leech\n- **Habitat:** stagnant Scáthfenn backwaters, battle sites, and Shadowfen drains\n- **Typical Level:** 5–12\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A forearm-long blood leech that clusters around carrion and mana-contaminated water. It cleans dead flesh rapidly but becomes aggressive around fresh wounds.\n- **Combat Traits:** blood scent, numbing bite, swelling drain, detaches under salt, heat, or anti-parasite magic.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Corpse-Reed Anticoagulant**.\n\n### Fen Widow\n- **Habitat:** willow thickets, hollow ruins, and elevated Scáthfenn ground\n- **Typical Level:** 12–22\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A long-legged marsh spider that stretches nearly invisible webs above flood height and feeds on giant insects, birds, and small beasts. Its colonies relocate before major inundation.\n- **Combat Traits:** water-walking, binding web, venom bite, vibration tracking.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Fen Widow Silk**.\n\n### Bog Wyrm\n- **Habitat:** deep Scáthfenn peat basins and beneath the Sunken Road\n- **Typical Level:** 22–34\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A limbless marsh dragon that tunnels through peat, opening waterways and swallowing concentrations of dangerous swamp mana. Its arrival can save one village from flooding while drowning another road.\n- **Combat Traits:** peat burrow, acidic breath, tail surge, mud camouflage, strong poison resistance.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Bog Wyrm Bile-Stone**.\n\n### Wisp Heron\n- **Habitat:** Witchlight Hollow and open Scáthfenn shallows\n- **Typical Level:** 6–14\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A tall grey bird that hunts fish beneath wandering lights, using the wisps as illumination without controlling them. Its arrival often means a pool contains ordinary prey rather than a disguised hazard.\n- **Combat Traits:** silent flight, precise spear-beak, false-light plumage, patient evasion.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Wisp Heron Plume**.\n\n## Caelvir Ancient Forest\n\n### Silverhorn Hart\n- **Habitat:** Caelvir glades, World-Tree rootwoods, and Moonsilver approaches\n- **Typical Level:** 6–14\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A silver-barked forest deer that browses invasive spirit growth and carries luminous moss between groves on its antlers. Elven wardens protect breeding herds and permit only limited hunts.\n- **Combat Traits:** forest sprint, antler sweep, root-step over difficult ground, herd alarm.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Silverhorn Cast Antler**.\n\n### Thornback Lynx\n- **Habitat:** Caelvir border forest and Feralglen beast trails\n- **Typical Level:** 10–20\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A large forest cat whose shoulder fur hardens into leaf-shaped quills. It hunts sick deer and root-rats, then sleeps high in silver-barked trees where its coat resembles dead vine.\n- **Combat Traits:** canopy pounce, thorn-quill flare, silent stalk, short-range bark camouflage.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Thornback Quill**.\n\n### Moonpetal Moth\n- **Habitat:** Moonsilver Glade, Spiritwell, and night-blooming Caelvir groves\n- **Typical Level:** 3–8\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A handspan moth whose silver wings pollinate flowers that open only under moonlight. Large emergences mark healthy spirit circulation and draw owls, bats, and forest sprites.\n- **Combat Traits:** silver dust cloud, light distraction, swarm evasion; harmless unless magically disturbed.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Moonpetal Wingdust**.\n\n### Rootcoil Serpent\n- **Habitat:** Caelvir root tunnels, Palebark Ruins, and the Whispering Maze\n- **Typical Level:** 14–26\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A thick green-brown constrictor that sleeps wound around warm elder roots and hunts burrowing monsters. It senses damage to living wood through its belly scales and becomes aggressive near wounded trees.\n- **Combat Traits:** root camouflage, constriction, wood-sense, soporific musk.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Rootcoil Scent Gland**.\n\n### Barkmantle Bear\n- **Habitat:** deep Caelvir, Feralglen, and old ruin margins\n- **Typical Level:** 20–32\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A huge omnivore whose fur hosts moss, beetles, and seed. It turns fallen logs, opens insect colonies, and creates clearings used by dozens of smaller species; adults attack mainly around cubs or contested food.\n- **Combat Traits:** bark-like hide, crushing forelimbs, roar, remarkable scent, regenerative moss layer.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Barkmantle Moss-Hide**.\n\n### Whisperwing Owl\n- **Habitat:** Caelvir canopy, Verdant Archive outskirts, and living labyrinths\n- **Typical Level:** 8–16\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A pale owl whose wing edges carry sound away from its body, allowing it to hunt root-rats and spell-moths in complete silence. Elven scholars read its nesting choices as evidence of quiet, stable branches—not prophecy.\n- **Combat Traits:** silent flight, echo redirection, talon dive, excellent magic-sensitive hearing.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Whisperwing Flight Feather**.\n\n## Muirscáth Coast and Sea\n\n### Tideglass Crab\n- **Habitat:** Muirscáth tide pools, Coralmarket reefs, and harbor pilings\n- **Typical Level:** 3–8\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A translucent crab that grazes magical algae from stone and coral. At low tide its shell refracts sunlight into moving blue-green patterns, making colonies easy to spot and difficult to count.\n- **Combat Traits:** sideways burst, glass claw, shell camouflage, group scatter.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Tideglass Carapace**.\n\n### Reefback Turtle\n- **Habitat:** Muirscáth reefs, island shallows, and Coralmarket waters\n- **Typical Level:** 8–16\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A broad sea turtle whose shell supports living coral and small fish. It carries reef fragments between islands and surfaces near docks where sailors scrape harmful growth without damaging the shell.\n- **Combat Traits:** armored retreat, heavy flipper strike, long breath, reef camouflage.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Reefback Coral Plate**.\n\n### Brinecoil Eel\n- **Habitat:** Muirscáth estuaries, Drifthollow caves, and flooded tunnels\n- **Typical Level:** 12–22\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A thick blue-black eel that stores charge from tidal mana and hunts in narrow submerged channels. Schools keep aggressive cave fish under control but become dangerous when storms overcharge the water.\n- **Combat Traits:** electric discharge, coil restraint, darkness sense, mud retreat.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Brinecoil Capacitor Organ**.\n\n### Stormray\n- **Habitat:** open Muirscáth sea lanes and Stormhaven cliffs\n- **Typical Level:** 18–30\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A manta-like aerial sea creature that rides pressure fronts just above the waves and feeds on storm insects and charged spray. Flocks often precede squalls by several hours.\n- **Combat Traits:** gliding dive, thunderclap wingbeat, static veil, wave-skimming escape.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Stormray Sail**.\n\n### Coral Mimic\n- **Habitat:** Muirscáth reefs, wrecks, and Drowned Temple approaches\n- **Typical Level:** 15–25\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A colonial predator that resembles harmless coral until warmth and vibration bring its feeding mouths open. It filters water between meals and becomes a serious harbor hazard when attached to pilings or hulls.\n- **Combat Traits:** perfect stationary camouflage, grasping polyps, numbing sting, colony regeneration.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Mimic Coral Nodule**.\n\n### Deepwake Leviathan\n- **Habitat:** far Muirscáth waters beyond ordinary fishing lanes\n- **Typical Level:** 40–60\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** An immense pelagic predator that follows deep mana currents and surfaces only during migration, injury, or pursuit of equally massive prey. Its passage reshapes fisheries for weeks and attracts every scavenger in the sea.\n- **Combat Traits:** ship-breaking mass, pressure roar, abyssal dive, tidal wake, high resistance to ordinary weapons.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Deepwake Pressure Plate**.",
