  "aerfala-bestiary-frontiers-and-deepgate": {
    "text": "# Aerfála Bestiary — Marches, Demon Realm, Steppe, and Deepgate\n\nAerfála's creatures belong to living habitats, food webs, economies, and local cultures. Predators hunt prey, herbivores migrate, scavengers follow death, monsters compete for territory, dungeon spawn follows Deepgate's established rules, and constructs or undead persist through the concrete magic that sustains them. A creature exists where its biology, origin, migration, summoning, breeding, dungeon generation, or actual movement places it—not merely because the player entered a scene.\n\n## Encounter and Knowledge Rules\n- Listed levels describe typical healthy specimens. Age, injury, mutation, pack size, training, habitat, dungeon depth, and established magic change an individual without granting arbitrary boss immunity.\n- Temperament follows hunger, nesting, fear, territory, injury, domestication, magical influence, and prior contact. Wildlife flees, watches, feeds, fights, mates, sleeps, migrates, or ignores travelers according to circumstance.\n- Identification requires sight, tracks, remains, expertise, records, local knowledge, magic with an established scope, or another real information path. Seeing a creature does not reveal its name, level, abilities, weaknesses, origin, or loot automatically.\n- Creature abilities resolve through actual stats, ranks, positioning, resistances, conditions, and rolls. Names such as basilisk, leviathan, or aberrant grant no hidden immunity.\n- Signature loot enters play only when physically obtained. A kill does not automatically place intact materials in inventory. Damage, harvesting skill, tools, time, decomposition, contamination, law, ownership, and local custom determine condition and quantity.\n- Natural sheds, molts, antlers, feathers, secretions, nests, and remains exist without killing. Hunting pressure changes local populations, prices, predator behavior, and prey numbers. Rare or mythic creatures do not respawn merely to replenish loot.\n- Ordinary meat, bone, hide, fat, organs, and trophies exist when anatomy and condition support them. Signature loot below names the material with a dedicated Items entry; it does not erase ordinary physical remains.\n- Guild rank affects legal commissions, pay, clearance, and institutional response. It does not physically prevent an adventurer from encountering a stronger creature outside Guild authority.\n\n## Fálgarr Marches\n\n### Howling Direwolf\n- **Habitat:** Fálgarr Marches hills and The Howling Hollow\n- **Typical Level:** 8–18\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A rangy grey pack predator whose throat chambers resonate with cave wind. Packs hunt hill deer and tunnel vermin; displaced packs follow trade roads when dens are disturbed.\n- **Combat Traits:** coordinated flank, resonant howl that disorients at close range, pursuit endurance, scent tracking.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Howling Direwolf Throat-Ring**.\n\n### Bramblehide Boar\n- **Habitat:** Fálgarr thickets, abandoned fields, and watchtower ruins\n- **Typical Level:** 10–20\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A heavy boar whose hide traps living thorn runners that protect it from large predators. Its rooting clears dense bramble and exposes old roads, but a frightened animal becomes a rolling wall of hooked vine.\n- **Combat Traits:** thorned charge, vine snag, mud armor, relentless short pursuit.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Bramblehide Thorn-Leather**.\n\n### Aqueduct Crawler\n- **Habitat:** pre-Collapse channels beneath the Fálgarr Marches\n- **Typical Level:** 12–22\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A pale many-legged amphibian that scrapes mineral growth and carrion from ancient waterworks. Colonies keep channels open until overpopulation strips ward mortar and causes leaks.\n- **Combat Traits:** wall adhesion, constricting body, mineral spit, vibration swarm response.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Crawler Adhesive Pad**.\n\n### Gilded Chimera\n- **Habitat:** The Gilded Ruins and nearby Marches\n- **Typical Level:** 22–35\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A magically bred predator descended from experiments in the ruined manor: lionlike forequarters, goatlike climbing legs, and a serpent tail sharing one unstable mana core. It has no natural breeding population beyond escaped or replicated specimens.\n- **Combat Traits:** multi-angle attack, fire breath, venomous tail, climbing charge, unstable core surge.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Gilded Chimera Core**.\n\n### Crypt Drowned\n- **Habitat:** The Sunken Crypt and flooded Marches tombs\n- **Typical Level:** 8–18\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A waterlogged undead body animated by old burial wards and residual intent. It waits motionless in flooded corridors, adding no natural ecology beyond concentrating rot, grave magic, and scavengers around the tomb.\n- **Combat Traits:** still-water ambush, grappling drag, pain immunity, grave-cold touch, vulnerability to consecration and drying heat.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Drowned Grave-Salt**.\n\n### Towerclaw Wyvern\n- **Habitat:** Bramblewatch Tower and northern Marches ridges\n- **Typical Level:** 16–28\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A lean cliff wyvern that nests in ruined towers because stone height protects its eggs from ground predators. It hunts goats, wolves, and unattended pack animals across a wide territory.\n- **Combat Traits:** cliff launch, talon carry, venom barb, masonry camouflage, territorial scream.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Towerclaw Wyvern Barb**.\n\n## Bréanriv Lowlands\n\n### River Drake\n- **Habitat:** Bréanriv waterways, Riversplit, and wooded tributaries\n- **Typical Level:** 8–18\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A dog-sized blue-green drake that hunts fish, waterfowl, and riverside pests. Family groups defend gravel nesting bars and are tolerated near farms because they drive off larger aquatic monsters.\n- **Combat Traits:** water sprint, tail slap, spray breath, cooperative nesting defense.\n- **Signature Loot:** **River Drake Keel Scale**.\n\n### Barrow Hound\n- **Habitat:** Battlefield Barrows and old Bréanriv war roads\n- **Typical Level:** 10–22\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A spectral war-dog reconstructed from repeated battlefield memory. It patrols routes between cairns and attacks grave robbers, active necromancy, or anyone carrying the scent of disturbed bones.\n- **Combat Traits:** mist body, pack manifestation, fear-bark, grave-scent, dispersal under strong sunlight or funerary rites.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Barrow Hound Grave-Iron**.\n\n### Redthorn Stag\n- **Habitat:** Bréanriv wooded hills and Redthorn Keep surroundings\n- **Typical Level:** 6–14\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A russet stag whose antlers host the same red thorn vine that covers the old keep. It browses aggressively on young growth and carries vine seed across the lowlands without suffering the poison.\n- **Combat Traits:** antler rake, thorn scatter, woodland leap, toxin resistance.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Redthorn Velvet**.\n\n### Gorge Wyvern\n- **Habitat:** The Gorge and southern Bréanriv cliffs\n- **Typical Level:** 20–32\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A broad-winged ambush wyvern that uses canyon thermals to remain aloft with little effort. It preys on goats, horses, and caravan animals, creating profitable but dangerous Guild culls.\n- **Combat Traits:** thermal glide, rock-drop, wing buffet, crushing jaws, canyon echo sense.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Gorge Wyvern Wing-Rib**.\n\n### Millfield Slime\n- **Habitat:** Bréanriv farms, millraces, and Greenmeadow irrigation\n- **Typical Level:** 1–5\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A translucent green slime that consumes spoiled grain, algae, and organic waste around mills. Healthy colonies are useful; overfed colonies divide rapidly and clog waterwheels.\n- **Combat Traits:** acidic digestion limited to soft organic matter, split under blunt force, water-current movement.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Millfield Slime Gel**.\n\n### Battlefield Carrion Crow\n- **Habitat:** Battlefield Barrows and Bréanriv memorial fields\n- **Typical Level:** 4–10\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A large black crow that feeds on grave insects and fragments of regenerating undead tissue. Flocks become agitated before the barrows stir, giving nearby villages a practical warning.\n- **Combat Traits:** mob harassment, grave-magic resistance, object theft, alarm flocking.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Carrion Crow Gravefeather**.\n\n## Demon Realm\n\n### Ashmane Hound\n- **Habitat:** Demon Realm steppe, borderlands, and military roads\n- **Typical Level:** 15–25\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A lean pack hunter with charcoal fur and a mane that smolders when excited. Demon caravans sometimes raise bonded lines, while wild packs hunt miasma grazers and battlefield carrion.\n- **Combat Traits:** pack pursuit, ash cloud, ember bite, emotional scenting limited to present bodily cues.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Ashmane Emberfur**.\n\n### Miasma Viper\n- **Habitat:** Demon Realm violet forests, dark rivers, and ruin margins\n- **Typical Level:** 18–28\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A long iridescent serpent that metabolizes concentrated miasma and keeps vent-fed rodent populations controlled. Its venom amplifies the victim's strongest current emotion while attacking the nerves.\n- **Combat Traits:** emotion-amplifying venom, branch glide, miasma camouflage, constricting retreat.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Miasma Viper Venom**.\n\n### Obsidian Carapace Beetle\n- **Habitat:** Demon Realm volcanic plains and obsidian mountain roots\n- **Typical Level:** 12–22\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A pony-sized beetle that eats brittle volcanic glass and excretes smoother road-grade stone. Colonies make dangerous terrain passable but defend feeding grounds by rolling heated shards.\n- **Combat Traits:** obsidian armor, shard roll, crushing mandibles, heat resistance.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Obsidian Beetle Carapace**.\n\n### Sulfur Drake\n- **Habitat:** Sulfur Flats, geothermal ravines, and Demon Realm vent fields\n- **Typical Level:** 24–38\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A yellow-black drake that nests beside miasma vents and feeds on mineral-shelled prey. Its digging keeps vents open; killing too many can cause pressure eruptions.\n- **Combat Traits:** sulfur breath, acid spit, vent dive, heat and miasma resistance.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Sulfur Drake Lungstone**.\n\n### Velvet Maw\n- **Habitat:** deep Demon Realm black-violet forests\n- **Typical Level:** 26–40\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A six-legged ambush beast covered in light-drinking velvet fur, with a flowerlike jaw hidden beneath a blunt face. It culls miasma-sick grazers and follows intense noise rather than morality or fear.\n- **Combat Traits:** light absorption, silent rush, radial bite, miasma pulse, poor vision in bright mortal sunlight.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Velvet Maw Pelt**.\n\n### Cinderfin Leviathan\n- **Habitat:** Demon Realm volcanic coast and the Sulfur Docks sea lanes\n- **Typical Level:** 35–50\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A black-red marine predator that swims through acidic, ash-warmed water and feeds on vent shoals. Its migration forces ships to use marked channels and replenishes coastal mineral beds through shed scales.\n- **Combat Traits:** acid-water immunity, cinder spray, hull ram, deep dive, miasma sonar.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Cinderfin Scale Slab**.\n\n## Sunmane Steppe\n\n### Sunhorn Antelope\n- **Habitat:** Sunmane Plains and seasonal steppe routes\n- **Typical Level:** 4–12\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A swift golden antelope whose translucent horn tips warm at sunrise. Herds crop the fastest grass, follow rain lines, and form the base prey of many steppe predators.\n- **Combat Traits:** burst sprint, herd feint, horn jab, long-distance weather sense.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Sunhorn Tip**.\n\n### Thunderhoof Bison\n- **Habitat:** Sunmane Plains and the Moot's outer grazing country\n- **Typical Level:** 12–24\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A massive dark bison whose hooves build static across dry grass. Herd migrations press firebreaks into the steppe and fertilize the routes used by clan livestock.\n- **Combat Traits:** herd charge, thunder-stomp, static hide, protective ring around calves.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Thunderhoof Horn**.\n\n### Plateau Glider\n- **Habitat:** Kithwood Rise and forested Sunmane plateaus\n- **Typical Level:** 6–14\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A fox-sized mammal with broad skin sails between its limbs, nesting in red-barked trees and feeding on fruit, insects, and resin. Colonies spread plateau seed across otherwise separated groves.\n- **Combat Traits:** silent glide, resin spit, canopy scramble, flock alarm.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Plateau Glider Sail**.\n\n### Painted Gorge Lion\n- **Habitat:** Painted Gorge ledges and red canyon country\n- **Typical Level:** 16–28\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A tawny cliff lion marked with ochre stripes that match the gorge walls. It hunts antelope and cliff goats, and its territories shape the safest warren and herd routes.\n- **Combat Traits:** ledge pounce, dust camouflage, crushing forepaw, territorial roar.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Painted Lion Mane**.\n\n### Embermane Direwolf\n- **Habitat:** eastern Sunmane Steppe and Emberhunt border country\n- **Typical Level:** 18–30\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A large red-black wolf whose mane sparks when the pack accelerates. Packs hunt bison calves, gorge beasts, and raiders' abandoned livestock, competing directly with Emberhunt hunters.\n- **Combat Traits:** pack encirclement, spark trail, heat bite, relentless pursuit.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Embermane Sparkfur**.\n\n### Redland Wyvern\n- **Habitat:** Sunmane painted canyons and eastern escarpments\n- **Typical Level:** 24–36\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A rust-red wyvern that nests on heated cliff faces and hunts across both steppe and gorge. Its abandoned nests become mineral-rich shelters for smaller gliders and birds.\n- **Combat Traits:** thermal soar, red-dust breath, tail hook, prey carry, cliff camouflage.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Redland Wyvern Scale**.\n\n## Deepgate Labyrinth\n\n### Threshold Gel\n- **Habitat:** Deepgate floors 1–10\n- **Typical Level:** 1–6\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A green-lit dungeon organism generated to consume refuse, corpses, and loose mana in upper tunnels. It follows moisture and reforms around dropped material, making it useful to the labyrinth and dangerous to sleeping delvers.\n- **Combat Traits:** engulf, mild acid, split under cutting force, attraction to loose mana.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Threshold Gel Nucleus**.\n\n### Sporeback Stalker\n- **Habitat:** Deepgate fungal biomes on floors 11–30\n- **Typical Level:** 10–20\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A low six-legged predator plated in living mushrooms that release spores after it feeds. It hunts by heat and vibration through fungal forests that should not fit underground.\n- **Combat Traits:** spore veil, heat tracking, wall crawl, fungal regeneration in native terrain.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Sporeback Colony Plate**.\n\n### Drowned Armor\n- **Habitat:** Deepgate drowned halls on floors 11–30\n- **Typical Level:** 16–26\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** An empty suit of dungeon-grown armor moved by water pressure and a knot of blue mana. It patrols submerged thresholds and reconstructs itself from compatible metal unless its core knot is removed.\n- **Combat Traits:** underwater mobility, weapon imitation, pressure grapple, metal reconstruction.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Drowned Armor Core-Knot**.\n\n### Crystal Maw\n- **Habitat:** Deepgate crystal caverns on middle and lower floors\n- **Typical Level:** 24–36\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A blind quadruped with a jaw of resonant crystal, generated where mana veins become overgrown. It eats crystal, metal, and enchanted gear, keeping the labyrinth's deposits in motion.\n- **Combat Traits:** resonance bite, shard roar, magic-item scent, reflective hide.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Crystal Maw Resonator**.\n\n### Map-Eater\n- **Habitat:** Deepgate floors 31 and below\n- **Typical Level:** 30–45\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A flat parchment-pale creature that crawls along walls and consumes marks, labels, trail paint, and weak spatial memory. It does not eat knowledge from minds; it erases physical navigation aids and deposits them as shifting patterns on its back.\n- **Combat Traits:** mark consumption, wall flattening, false trail display, ambush fold.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Map-Eater Skin**.\n\n### Vaultborn Aberrant\n- **Habitat:** deepest confirmed Deepgate floors and Sealed Vault approaches\n- **Typical Level:** 45–65\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A Pre-Collapse-touched organism assembled from dungeon matter around geometry that does not belong in the current world. No two specimens share a body plan, and their presence causes nearby spawn to deform.\n- **Combat Traits:** variable anatomy, spatial rupture, adaptive resistance limited by observed damage, core instability.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Vaultborn Paradox Core**.\n\n",
