  "demi-plane-bestiary": {
    "text": "# Demi-Plane Bestiary\n\nThe Demi-Plane's fauna is part of Tsukiko's designed fox-realm ecology. These creatures are native animals, spirit-beasts, elemental life, or defensive organisms rather than an added sapient population. They form pollination, migration, predation, decomposition, water regulation, mana moderation, boundary maintenance, and seed-distribution cycles across the fixed 5×5 region grid. They do not create villages, factions, shops, dialogue networks, or unexplained societies.\n\n## Realm-Specific Rules\n- Access remains governed by Demi-Plane Gate, the Demi-Plane Anchor, Tsukiko's permission, and established intrusion exceptions. Native fauna cannot carry outsiders through those rules.\n- Creatures know their habitat, senses, learned routes, threats, and prior experiences. They do not know Tsukiko's secrets, visitor histories, distant events, character sheets, or narrator information.\n- The fixed biomes, coordinates, map tiles, locations, development categories, Mana Heart, Foundation Ridge, Grey Boundary, and Last Edge anchor remain intact. Migration connects the tiles without rearranging them.\n- Most materials come from seasonal shedding, molting, cast antlers, empty shells, secretions, cocoons, natural death, or a real hunt. Sanctuary harvesting remains subject to Tsukiko's permission.\n- Population loss affects the realm. Removing pollinators, grazers, predators, decomposers, or boundary fauna produces persistent ecological consequences rather than automatic replacement.\n- Taming follows the established Tame and Tame Monster mechanics, the creature's temperament, actual interaction, ability scope, and resistance. A bestiary entry does not make every species tame, obedient, or available.\n- Typical levels describe normal specimens. Boundary stress, mana surplus, age, injury, and habitat alter an individual through established mechanics.\n\n## Northern Frost, Mist, and White Stone\n\n### Frost-Tail Fox\n- **Habitat:** The Still Frontier and Frostpine Ridge\n- **Typical Level:** 8–16\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A compact white fox whose tail holds blue-white frost foxfire instead of ordinary warmth. It caches frostpine cones along the advancing frontier, planting the first trees on newly stable ground.\n- **Combat Traits:** snow camouflage, cold immunity, foxfire feint, silent ridge sprint.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Frost-Tail Wintercoat**.\n\n### Glass-Antler Elk\n- **Habitat:** The Still Frontier, Pale Reaches, and seasonal routes into the Deep Expanse\n- **Typical Level:** 8–18\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A tall pale elk whose translucent antlers collect constellation lichen and frozen mana. Herds open paths through snow and carry northern spores south during their long migration.\n- **Combat Traits:** herd charge, antler-light scatter, snow endurance, boundary-weather sense.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Cast Glass Antler**.\n\n### Spiral Owl\n- **Habitat:** Frostpine Ridge and the northern Pale Reaches\n- **Typical Level:** 5–12\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A white-and-violet owl that rides the Demi-Plane's slowly spiraling snow, hunting fogmice and icewing insects without landing for hours.\n- **Combat Traits:** spiral dive, snowblind concealment, silent flight, breath-mist sight.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Spiral Owl Pinion**.\n\n### Fogmouse\n- **Habitat:** The Pale Reaches and Ghost Valleys\n- **Typical Level:** 1–3\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A pearl-grey mouse with translucent ears and a body that becomes indistinct inside dimensional mist. Colonies spread silver-lichen spores between otherwise bare stone benches.\n- **Combat Traits:** mist blending, rapid burrow, swarm scatter; harmless.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Fogmouse Whisker**.\n\n### Stoneback Grazer\n- **Habitat:** The Pale Reaches and western Fold\n- **Typical Level:** 10–18\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A low quadruped whose layered hide resembles the white stone benches it feeds upon. It scrapes mineral crust loose, opening habitat for lichen, insects, and temporary ghost flora.\n- **Combat Traits:** stone camouflage, shoulder shove, mineral hide, immobile defensive crouch.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Stoneback Plate**.\n\n### Veil Skate\n- **Habitat:** The Pale Reaches and Veiled Edge\n- **Typical Level:** 10–20\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A translucent ray-shaped creature that glides a handspan above stone or grass, feeding on silver spores and loose boundary light. Its migration links the Reaches' mist cycle to the Edge's aurora scrub.\n- **Combat Traits:** low glide, light-drain pass, translucent camouflage, tail lash.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Veil-Skate Membrane**.\n\n## Shining Channels and Folded Country\n\n### Reed Elk\n- **Habitat:** The North Field and Threshold March\n- **Typical Level:** 6–14\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A blue-grey elk with translucent reedlike antlers that wades the Shining Channels and crops old rivergrass. Its hooves press seed into wet banks without collapsing them.\n- **Combat Traits:** water charge, channel leap, herd alarm, moving-water sense.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Luminous Reed Velvet**.\n\n### Lantern Goose\n- **Habitat:** The North Field, Threshold March, and Mirror Mere migrations\n- **Typical Level:** 3–8\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A broad-winged waterbird whose belly glows through its feathers at dusk. Flocks carry luminous reed-seed and aquatic spores between channels, paths, and twilight pools.\n- **Combat Traits:** flash-wing distraction, flock alarm, strong migration memory, water takeoff.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Lantern Goose Down**.\n\n### Channel Serpent\n- **Habitat:** Shining Channels and North Field wetlands\n- **Typical Level:** 12–22\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A sleek silver-blue river serpent that keeps ribbonfin shoals from stripping young reed roots. It follows waterways even when they move underground and surfaces where prey becomes overabundant.\n- **Combat Traits:** current burst, constriction, water-sense, reflective scale decoy.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Channel Serpent Scale**.\n\n### Fold-Marten\n- **Habitat:** The Fold and Returning Valley\n- **Typical Level:** 8–16\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A long copper-brown animal that enters narrow terrain creases and emerges from another connected fold with nuts, eggs, or stolen objects. Its caches move plant seed between distant slopes.\n- **Combat Traits:** short fold-step through existing terrain creases, agile bite, decoy trail, excellent memory for connected folds.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Fold-Marten Fur**.\n\n### Pleatback Tortoise\n- **Habitat:** The Fold, Returning Valley, and nearby scrub\n- **Typical Level:** 10–18\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A slow tortoise with a shell arranged in overlapping geometric pleats. It grazes the warm and cool faces of folded ridges, carrying seed between microclimates.\n- **Combat Traits:** folded shell defense, slope-locking claws, short adjacency shift when fully withdrawn.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Pleatback Scute**.\n\n### Loop Hound\n- **Habitat:** The Fold's ridges and returning paths\n- **Typical Level:** 14–24\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A lean ink-grey pack hunter that uses the Fold's loops to pressure stoneback grazers without exhausting a single herd. It never teleports; it knows routes other creatures fail to recognize.\n- **Combat Traits:** loop ambush, pack relay, returning pursuit, spatial scenting.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Loop Hound Sinew**.\n\n## Veiled Edge and Fox Sanctuary\n\n### Aurora Hare\n- **Habitat:** The Veiled Edge and eastern Fold\n- **Typical Level:** 5–12\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A silver hare whose fur absorbs ground-aurora color while it grazes old spirit-grass. Its rapid movement sends warning ripples through the luminous scrub.\n- **Combat Traits:** color-shift camouflage, light burst, boundary-sensitive flight response.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Aurora Hare Fur**.\n\n### Veil Moth\n- **Habitat:** The Veiled Edge and Shimmering Curtain\n- **Typical Level:** 4–10\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A large translucent moth that rests directly against the boundary and pollinates glass-leaf scrub. Its wings darken before outside pressure reaches the ward network.\n- **Combat Traits:** boundary cling, prism dust, light camouflage, pressure-sensitive swarm.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Veil Moth Wing**.\n\n### Boundary Walker\n- **Habitat:** The Veiled Edge\n- **Typical Level:** 20–30\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A rare, faceless long-legged grazer shaped like a deer, feeding on dense ground-light without crossing the Curtain. When boundary pressure changes, every visible Walker aligns toward its source.\n- **Combat Traits:** aurora stride, light-drain, silent kick, partial translucence, coordinated warning posture.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Boundary Walker Hoofglass**.\n\n### Velvet Fox\n- **Habitat:** Veiled Fox Sanctuary\n- **Typical Level:** 6–14\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A small black, white, or russet sanctuary fox whose tail-tip holds a harmless lantern glow. It buries fallen fruit, spreads tree seed, and sleeps along warm mycelial channels.\n- **Combat Traits:** foxfire decoy, root-path navigation, silent brush movement, strong ward recognition without secret knowledge.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Velvet Fox Shedfur**.\n\n### Moon-Antler Deer\n- **Habitat:** Veiled Fox Sanctuary and its private woodland margins\n- **Typical Level:** 10–20\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A pale deer with crescent antlers that prunes young sanctuary trees and distributes sacred berry seed. Herds announce unfamiliar movement with a low bell-like call.\n- **Combat Traits:** crescent antler sweep, moonlit camouflage, ward-safe pathing, herd alarm.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Moon-Antler Velvet**.\n\n### Violetwing Moth\n- **Habitat:** Veiled Fox Sanctuary and First Meadow\n- **Typical Level:** 3–8\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A palm-sized moth with transparent wings veined in violet foxfire. It carries pollen between sanctuary night-blooms and Meadow flowers, keeping the two plant communities connected.\n- **Combat Traits:** foxfire attraction, gentle light veil, swarm evasion; non-hostile.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Violetwing Glass**.\n\n## First Meadow, Threshold March, and Stone Rise\n\n### Duskbee\n- **Habitat:** The First Meadow and Westreach flowerbanks\n- **Typical Level:** 1–4\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A thumb-sized bee that builds translucent comb beneath grass hummocks and pollinates blooms opening between daylight and foxfire. Colonies are calm away from the comb and defensive around winter stores.\n- **Combat Traits:** swarm defense, warm-light trail, coordinated pollination; individually weak.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Dusk Honey**.\n\n### Lantern Crane\n- **Habitat:** Threshold March, North Field, and Mirror Mere\n- **Typical Level:** 6–14\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A tall pearl-grey crane with a warm throat-light that follows the realm's main water and mana corridors. Resting flocks move seed and small aquatic life between wetlands.\n- **Combat Traits:** spear-beak, flash call, long glide, route memory.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Lantern Crane Plume**.\n\n### Path Beetle\n- **Habitat:** Threshold March and Heartgate Basin paths\n- **Typical Level:** 1–5\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A hand-sized pearl beetle that loosens compacted soil around living mana channels and consumes roots damaged by heavy traffic. Trails shift around its nesting patches.\n- **Combat Traits:** burrow, shell curl, mana-flow attraction; harmless.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Path Beetle Carapace**.\n\n### Moss-Horn Goat\n- **Habitat:** The Stone Rise\n- **Typical Level:** 8–16\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A sure-footed grey goat whose curled horns support lichen and moss. Herds move spores between terraces and abandon stone under dangerous pressure before visible cracks form.\n- **Combat Traits:** cliff balance, horn ram, scree kick, structural vibration sense.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Moss-Horn Curl**.\n\n### Spring Snail\n- **Habitat:** Stone Rise mineral springs\n- **Typical Level:** 2–6\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A translucent fist-sized snail that grazes crystal moss and concentrates trace minerals into a spiral shell. It abandons the shell unharmed when the inner whorls fill.\n- **Combat Traits:** mineral filtering, shell retreat, adhesive foot; non-hostile.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Spring-Snail Pearl Shell**.",
