    "text": "# Demi-Plane Bestiary — Mirror Waters, Outer Reaches, and Boundaries\n\nThe Demi-Plane's fauna is part of Tsukiko's designed fox-realm ecology. These creatures are native animals, spirit-beasts, elemental life, or defensive organisms rather than an added sapient population. They form pollination, migration, predation, decomposition, water regulation, mana moderation, boundary maintenance, and seed-distribution cycles across the fixed 5×5 region grid. They do not create villages, factions, shops, dialogue networks, or unexplained societies.\n\n## Realm-Specific Rules\n- Access remains governed by Demi-Plane Gate, the Demi-Plane Anchor, Tsukiko's permission, and established intrusion exceptions. Native fauna cannot carry outsiders through those rules.\n- Creatures know their habitat, senses, learned routes, threats, and prior experiences. They do not know Tsukiko's secrets, visitor histories, distant events, character sheets, or narrator information.\n- The fixed biomes, coordinates, map tiles, locations, development categories, Mana Heart, Foundation Ridge, Grey Boundary, and Last Edge anchor remain intact. Migration connects the tiles without rearranging them.\n- Most materials come from seasonal shedding, molting, cast antlers, empty shells, secretions, cocoons, natural death, or a real hunt. Sanctuary harvesting remains subject to Tsukiko's permission.\n- Population loss affects the realm. Removing pollinators, grazers, predators, decomposers, or boundary fauna produces persistent ecological consequences rather than automatic replacement.\n- Taming follows the established Tame and Tame Monster mechanics, the creature's temperament, actual interaction, ability scope, and resistance. A bestiary entry does not make every species tame, obedient, or available.\n- Typical levels describe normal specimens. Boundary stress, mana surplus, age, injury, and habitat alter an individual through established mechanics.\n\n## Mirror Water, Quiet Shore, Westreach, Heartgate, and Dawn Barrow\n\n### Moonfin\n- **Habitat:** Mirror Mere and Dawn Stream headwaters\n- **Typical Level:** 2–8\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A silver-lilac fish that grazes luminous algae and disturbs mirror-lotus roots when stored mana must return to circulation. Shoals appear as moving thoughts beneath still water.\n- **Combat Traits:** reflection decoy, synchronized school turn, light feeding; harmless.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Mirrorfin Scale**.\n\n### Glass Frog\n- **Habitat:** Mirror Mere reed-beds and Low Reaches clean pools\n- **Typical Level:** 2–6\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A translucent frog whose organs glow in distinct colors while it digests insects and excess water mana. Chorus changes reveal water quality through observable biology rather than prophecy.\n- **Combat Traits:** transparent camouflage, flash pulse, adhesive leap, mild skin irritant.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Glass Frog Slough**.\n\n### Reflection Heron\n- **Habitat:** Mirror Mere and Dawn Barrow shallows\n- **Typical Level:** 8–16\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A long-legged twilight bird that moves nutrients between isolated pools. It strikes only after prey and reflection align, leaving one perfect ring on the surface.\n- **Combat Traits:** precise spear-beak, delayed reflection feint, stillness camouflage, shallow-water stride.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Reflection Heron Feather**.\n\n### Glass Crab\n- **Habitat:** Quiet Shore tideline\n- **Typical Level:** 4–10\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A clear many-legged shore grazer that sifts dimensional residue from moon-sand and retreats beneath the not-water without crossing the boundary.\n- **Combat Traits:** transparent shell, lateral burst, prism claw, sand burial.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Glass Crab Shell**.\n\n### Shellback Skate\n- **Habitat:** beneath the Quiet Shore's not-water\n- **Typical Level:** 12–22\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A broad ray-shaped creature that grazes reflected light below the still surface. Its seasonal shed becomes the shell crystal found along the strand.\n- **Combat Traits:** subsurface glide, pressure pulse, shell edge, not-water concealment.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Shell Crystal**.\n\n### Dewback Tortoise\n- **Habitat:** Westreach and First Meadow margins\n- **Typical Level:** 6–14\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A broad low tortoise whose shell collects foxfire dew in patterned channels. It carries seed, pollen, and fungal spores between young groves while grazing only mature groundcover.\n- **Combat Traits:** shell defense, dew flash, steady root-path navigation, powerful bite when threatened.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Dewback Scute**.\n\n### Brush-Tail Garden Fox\n- **Habitat:** Heartgate Basin and Verdant Plot\n- **Typical Level:** 4–10\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A small russet fox with a broad brush tail that buries fallen mana fruit, hunts crop pests, and sleeps beside warm root-streams. It is tame around established residents without being owned by default.\n- **Combat Traits:** root-path sprint, fruit-cache decoy, pest pounce, foxfire dust shake.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Brush-Tail Shedfur**.\n\n### Redscale Lizard\n- **Habitat:** Dawn Barrow redstone banks and Easthold margins\n- **Typical Level:** 4–12\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A coral-red lizard that basks on glowing streamstones and eats mana gnats emerging from warm water. Its burrows keep riverbank soil aerated.\n- **Combat Traits:** heat dash, tail-drop decoy, redstone camouflage, sharp bite.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Redscale Sheath**.\n\n## Marsh, Vale, Prairie, Easthold, and Rift\n\n### Dream Salamander\n- **Habitat:** Low Reaches nursery pools\n- **Typical Level:** 5–12\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A translucent green-blue amphibian that carries eggs between migrating pools and feeds on dream gnats drawn to surplus marsh potential. Its skin patterns respond to water quality.\n- **Combat Traits:** pool-to-pool leap, sleep-mist puff, toxin sensing, tail regeneration.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Dream-Salamander Sheath**.\n\n### Mossback Pangolin\n- **Habitat:** Hollow Vale terraces and Dim March approaches\n- **Typical Level:** 8–16\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A long-scaled insectivore whose mossy armor lets it sleep against terrace walls unseen. It prevents burrowing beetles from undermining clay banks.\n- **Combat Traits:** armored curl, digging claws, adhesive tongue, moss camouflage.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Mossback Scale**.\n\n### Grasswhale\n- **Habitat:** The Deep Expanse\n- **Typical Level:** 20–35\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** An immense gentle herbivore whose broad back barely rises above the tallest grass. Its infrasonic calls coordinate herd routes and vibrate mana amber into stable formation around deep roots.\n- **Combat Traits:** massive body, infrasonic call, grass-wave concealment, defensive herd circle; avoids combat.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Grasswhale Song Amber**.\n\n### Prairie Drake\n- **Habitat:** The Deep Expanse and Southroll margins\n- **Typical Level:** 16–28\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A long-winged drake that skims grass tops to flush insects and small prey, trimming tall growth with its wing edges. Display flights establish territory without constant lethal fighting.\n- **Combat Traits:** low glide, wing-shear, grassfire breath limited to short controlled bursts, aerial feint.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Prairie Drake Wingfilm**.\n\n### Gilt Scarab\n- **Habitat:** The Easthold\n- **Typical Level:** 3–8\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A golden beetle that consumes overheated mana-stone dust and buries it in cool foundation corridors. Colonies prevent the dry upland's heat cycle from becoming wildfire.\n- **Combat Traits:** heat resistance, reflective shell, dust burrow, group scatter.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Gilt Scarab Carapace**.\n\n### Rift Crawler\n- **Habitat:** Rift March fissures\n- **Typical Level:** 18–28\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A many-limbed blue-black climber that descends sheer walls head-first and grazes cold-light fungus. Its claws widen safe spore channels but can destabilize heavily mined faces.\n- **Combat Traits:** vertical sprint, gripping swarm, mineral spit, darkness camouflage.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Rift Crawler Claw**.\n\n### Bluejaw Cave Drake\n- **Habitat:** deep Rift March clefts\n- **Typical Level:** 22–34\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A compact dark drake with a cobalt-lit jaw that hunts crawlers and echo bats through thermal shafts. It is the clefts' principal predator and aggressively defends roosts.\n- **Combat Traits:** cold-blue breath, wall launch, crushing jaw, echo tracking, darkstone camouflage.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Bluejaw Drake Tooth**.\n\n## Dim and Southern Boundaries\n\n### Hush Moth\n- **Habitat:** The Dim March\n- **Typical Level:** 4–10\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A broad pale moth whose velvet wings absorb the minute vibrations used by Dim March fungi. It pollinates in complete silence and settles when foreign noise enters a hollow.\n- **Combat Traits:** sound-damping dust, silent flight, mass settling alarm, fragile body.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Hush-Moth Velvet**.\n\n### Shade-Beast\n- **Habitat:** deep Dim March moss banks\n- **Typical Level:** 18–30\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A large dormant predator that wakes when sustained noise drives burrowers from their normal layers. It hunts by vibration and returns to sleep once the hollow quiets.\n- **Combat Traits:** moss ambush, vibration sense, shadowed pounce, soporific breath, long dormancy.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Shade-Beast Dreamfur**.\n\n### Anchor Beetle\n- **Habitat:** The Grey Boundary\n- **Typical Level:** 5–12\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A dense grey beetle that packs anchor-stone grit into circular burrows across the moor. Thousands of colonies distribute minute stabilizing forces through the fixed southern border.\n- **Combat Traits:** spatial resistance, armored curl, grit spray, unmovable brace when burrowed.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Anchor Beetle Casing**.\n\n### Sky Ray\n- **Habitat:** The Open Horizon\n- **Typical Level:** 10–20\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A pale ray-shaped creature that drifts at eye height on broad atmospheric currents, feeding on windseed and airborne mana. Schools carry seed between the savanna and Deep Expanse.\n- **Combat Traits:** air glide, pressure pulse, mirage underside, coordinated turn.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Sky-Ray Sail**.\n\n### Pearl Moth\n- **Habitat:** The Fade and Dissolving Hills\n- **Typical Level:** 5–12\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A near-invisible moth that pollinates transparent boundary flowers and carries viable seed back toward solid ground. It appears as a mother-of-pearl gap in the mist.\n- **Combat Traits:** edge-loss camouflage, mist glide, fading dust, fragile on unfinished ground.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Pearl-Moth Silk**.\n\n### Fade-Beast\n- **Habitat:** the outer Fade\n- **Typical Level:** 22–32\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A pale many-jointed grazer that consumes unstable terrain outlines before they harden into dangerous malformed ground. It is shy around stable creatures but attacks attempts to bind unfinished shapes recklessly.\n- **Combat Traits:** outline feeding, partial intangibility, certainty-drain bite, mist retreat.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Fade-Beast Outline**.\n\n### Grey Needle-Fox\n- **Habitat:** The Last Edge\n- **Typical Level:** 12–22\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A rare narrow fox with stiff silver-grey guard hairs that drinks condensation from anchor seams and eats fixed-point beetles. Its tracks stop exactly where direction ceases.\n- **Combat Traits:** shadowless camouflage, needle-fur defense, fixed-route sprint, spatial pressure sense.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Needle-Fox Quillfur**.\n\n### Sentinel Moth\n- **Habitat:** The Last Edge during anchor stress\n- **Typical Level:** 20–30\n- **Ecology & Behavior:** A rare white moth that emerges only when the fixed coordinate begins to drift. Adults circle the Dimensional Anchor Point once, shed silver dust, and vanish when stability returns.\n- **Combat Traits:** drift sensing, spatially fixed flight path, silver warning cloud; avoids direct combat.\n- **Signature Loot:** **Sentinel-Moth Dust**.\n\n",
